Feature: The plane follows its telemetry
  The view shows the plane where its telemetry says it is, and at the same attitude. Before
  the first message, the view has no plane.

  Expectation: No telemetry, no plane
    Given the telemetry is silent
    When 1 second passes
    Then the plane in the view is missing

  Expectation: The plane is where it says it is
    Given the telemetry is flowing
    And the reported distance north of home is 120 m
    And the reported height is 40 m
    When 1 second passes
    Then the plane in the view is shown
    And the distance north of the pilot box in the view is 120 m
    And the height above the pilot box in the view is 40 m

  Expectation: The plane banks as it banks
    Given the telemetry is flowing
    And the reported bank is 30 degrees
    When 1 second passes
    Then the right wing in the view is low

  Expectation: The plane points where it flies
    Given the telemetry is flowing
    And the reported heading is east
    When 1 second passes
    Then the heading in the view is east

  Expectation: A quiet plane stays where it was last heard
    The view does not hide a plane when the telemetry stops. A lost link is often short, and
    the last position is the best guess.
    Given the telemetry is flowing
    And the reported distance north of home is 120 m
    And the plane in the view is shown
    When the telemetry is silent
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the plane in the view is shown
    And the distance north of the pilot box in the view is 120 m
